1
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:12,960
Brighten things up and try stepping away.

2
00:00:23,140 --> 00:00:28,460
Like someone calling
out to you after the rain.

3
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:35,340
Walking while looking back,
holding Gar-chan's hand.

4
00:00:35,340 --> 00:00:42,460
That strange feeling I had back then.

5
00:00:43,160 --> 00:00:47,720
So, on the tiles of the arcade street,

6
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:53,500
I tried walking only on the black ones.

7
00:00:55,860 --> 00:00:59,700
Everyone was a child once,

8
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:01,820
but everyone has forgotten.

9
00:01:02,760 --> 00:01:09,120
Pompous-faced politicians and
blue-eyeshadowed aunties too.

10
00:01:09,620 --> 00:01:14,380
Try turning that corner over there.

11
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:19,920
You can meet everyone, everyone.

12
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:27,840
Over there is Kame-ari
surely there's Kame-ari.

13
00:01:29,340 --> 00:01:33,020
Everyone, come on over to our town!

14
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:34,600
Thank you.

15
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:39,460
Tabimakase Hot Spring Tour

16
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:47,920
Wow, your performance in the other
day's competition was splendid.

17
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:50,520
I didn't expect you to
reach the green in two there.

18
00:01:50,520 --> 00:01:52,420
Pure luck, pure luck.

19
00:01:52,420 --> 00:01:55,180
Well, luck is part of skill, you know.

20
00:01:55,180 --> 00:01:56,280
You're too modest, Ohara-kun.

21
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:00,480
Congratulations.

22
00:02:00,480 --> 00:02:02,600
Congratulations, President.

23
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:04,040
Congratulations.

24
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:15,600
Congratulations, President,
on 25 years of the metal company.

25
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:17,860
On behalf of everyone, please.

26
00:02:17,860 --> 00:02:19,260
Please, go ahead.

27
00:02:21,540 --> 00:02:23,640
This travel invitation

28
00:02:24,260 --> 00:02:25,880
is from all of us common folk.

29
00:02:27,840 --> 00:02:31,040
It's a luxurious two-night, three-day
trip to a first-class hot spring hotel.

30
00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:34,880
And since it's a paired invitation,
Chief Ohara, please come along too.

31
00:02:35,860 --> 00:02:37,120
With Ohara-kun?

32
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:42,540
Chief Ohara is the great squad leader who keeps that Ryotsu in line,
after all.

33
00:02:42,540 --> 00:02:44,180
In appreciation of all your hard work.

34
00:02:44,180 --> 00:02:50,480
Since you're so comfortable with Chief Ohara,
we thought you could relax and really enjoy the trip.

35
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:53,060
Thank you, everyone.

36
00:02:53,560 --> 00:02:56,680
Well then, Ohara-kun,
we'll gratefully accept.

37
00:02:57,840 --> 00:02:59,420
We'd be honored to tag along.

38
00:03:03,380 --> 00:03:06,140
Wow, I'm glad they were so happy about it.

39
00:03:06,140 --> 00:03:07,600
Yeah, really.

40
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:09,560
By the way, where's Ryo-chan?

41
00:03:09,780 --> 00:03:12,580
Ryo-san went to pay for the travel tickets.

42
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Terai-san.

43
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:18,320
What did you just say?

44
00:03:18,320 --> 00:03:19,433
W-wh...

45
00:03:19,483 --> 00:03:22,780
I mean,
he went to pay the 300,000 yen for the trip.

46
00:03:22,780 --> 00:03:25,320
Didn't you say that was
supposed to be Terai-san's job?

47
00:03:25,320 --> 00:03:26,960
What about the payment?

48
00:03:27,840 --> 00:03:30,100
Why are you the one
talking about this, senpai?

49
00:03:31,100 --> 00:03:34,620
Well, Ryo-san insisted
that I be the one to go.

50
00:03:35,180 --> 00:03:36,400
So you paid 300,000 yen?

51
00:03:36,780 --> 00:03:38,240
You handed it over?

52
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:38,980
Y-yes.

53
00:03:41,060 --> 00:03:42,680
Me? Did I do something wrong?

54
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:44,580
You had your senior carry 300,000 yen!

55
00:03:44,720 --> 00:03:46,300
There's no way this ends well!

56
00:03:47,580 --> 00:03:49,960
Attention, please.
The race is about to start.

57
00:03:51,080 --> 00:03:54,500
Are you okay, Ryo-san? That was supposed to
be the money for the travel agency, right?

58
00:03:54,500 --> 00:03:57,920
Relax, I just borrowed about 300,000.

59
00:03:58,380 --> 00:04:01,780
Borrowed?
I put the whole thing on this one race!

60
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:04,840
It's a dead-certain race
with triple the payout!

61
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:09,240
If we win back 900,000, we can pay back the 300,000 from that.
No problem.

62
00:04:09,660 --> 00:04:12,780
The gates have opened,
and number 11 has made a beautiful start.

63
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:15,500
From the outside, the second favorite,
Harahorohire Harehare,

64
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:18,860
is following closely behind, with the
top favorite, Yama no Hope, right after.

65
00:04:19,580 --> 00:04:22,440
Yes! Good,
this is exactly the outcome I predicted!

66
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:26,160
Only 10 meters to the finish!
The 600,000 is ours!

67
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:34,520
An unexpected turn! The top favorite, Yama no Hope,
has been thrown just before the finish line!

68
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:40,280
What are we going to do, Ryo-san?
The 300,000 is gone! What now?

69
00:04:40,380 --> 00:04:44,200
Ouch! He got thrown, and I couldn't read that at all!
Damn it!

70
00:04:44,440 --> 00:04:46,260
This is going to count as embezzlement!

71
00:04:52,760 --> 00:04:53,480
Ryo-san

72
00:04:55,300 --> 00:04:56,660
You lost it on the horse races?

73
00:04:56,660 --> 00:04:58,900
Yeah, so you're completely broke?

74
00:04:58,900 --> 00:05:00,560
Why would you go and gamble on horses?

75
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:01,703
Well,

76
00:05:01,753 --> 00:05:06,080
I was only trying to give you two a more luxurious trip,
you know.

77
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:09,560
I put it all on a race that
was supposed to be a sure thing.

78
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:12,820
Things just don't go as planned, do they?
Life's like that.

79
00:05:12,820 --> 00:05:15,840
"Didn't go as planned" doesn't cut it,
you know!

80
00:05:16,220 --> 00:05:17,880
Yeah, don't just blame me!

81
00:05:17,880 --> 00:05:20,760
Besides, what about you?
You're the one who handed me the money!

82
00:05:23,440 --> 00:05:25,807
You should have been able to
predict how it would turn out,

83
00:05:25,857 --> 00:05:29,080
so what about your responsibility
for handing it over so carelessly?

84
00:05:30,520 --> 00:05:32,820
Yes, everyone's said that to me too.

85
00:05:33,260 --> 00:05:37,115
Right? But if this means
we can't go on the trip,

86
00:05:37,165 --> 00:05:40,020
we'd feel terrible toward the chief and the section chief,
wouldn't we?

87
00:05:40,900 --> 00:05:42,276
So then, Terai-kun.

88
00:05:42,326 --> 00:05:47,400
Let's cover the trip expenses
for those two poor fellows.

89
00:05:48,280 --> 00:05:52,280
No, but I have a home loan and all that,
so I barely have any pocket money.

90
00:05:53,440 --> 00:05:56,760
You've been secretly stashing away savings,
haven't you?

91
00:05:57,520 --> 00:06:00,000
The poor chief and section chief.

92
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:02,960
Because of someone,
the trip is going to be cancelled?

93
00:06:02,960 --> 00:06:05,400
They really are pitiful.

94
00:06:06,460 --> 00:06:08,460
Hot spring trip coupons.

95
00:06:09,080 --> 00:06:12,000
Yeah, get two with a budget
of 2,000 yen per person.

96
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:14,100
That's tough.

97
00:06:14,100 --> 00:06:17,800
Even for somewhere nearby,
2,000 yen is just not enough, no way.

98
00:06:18,580 --> 00:06:20,280
As long as it's cheap, I don't care.

99
00:06:20,280 --> 00:06:23,220
We don't need meals,
and we can even sleep outside.

100
00:06:24,040 --> 00:06:26,680
If it's a round-trip ski bus ticket,
we can somehow manage.

101
00:06:26,680 --> 00:06:28,800
Nice, yes, let's take that one.

102
00:06:32,360 --> 00:06:36,020
Chief and Section Chief,
please enjoy your relaxing hot spring trip.

103
00:06:36,780 --> 00:06:38,920
It's been a while, so I'll take it easy.

104
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:41,080
I'm counting on you all
to hold down the fort.

105
00:06:43,280 --> 00:06:44,800
But isn't the car running late?

106
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:45,780
Yeah, true.

107
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:48,820
Chief, Section Chief, this way, please.

108
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:51,880
We're waiting behind the car.

109
00:06:51,880 --> 00:06:53,400
Well, that makes sense.

110
00:06:53,780 --> 00:06:56,360
We should keep the front entrance open for emergencies,
after all.

111
00:06:56,360 --> 00:06:56,800
Yes, you're right.

112
00:06:58,580 --> 00:06:59,700
Well then, I'm off.

113
00:06:59,700 --> 00:07:00,880
Have a nice trip.

114
00:07:00,880 --> 00:07:03,120
Have a nice trip.

115
00:07:03,120 --> 00:07:05,420
Ryo-chan,
looks like you actually paid it in properly.

116
00:07:05,420 --> 00:07:08,120
Looks like we were worrying over nothing.

117
00:07:08,120 --> 00:07:10,480
Yeah, don't worry, it's fine.

118
00:07:13,880 --> 00:07:14,600
What is this?

119
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:16,040
What happened to the hired car?

120
00:07:16,040 --> 00:07:17,500
Well, if it were a hired car,

121
00:07:17,500 --> 00:07:19,920
we might get caught in traffic,

122
00:07:20,280 --> 00:07:22,780
so for now you'll travel to the bus by this.

123
00:07:23,020 --> 00:07:23,960
To the bus?

124
00:07:24,180 --> 00:07:27,280
Yes. A bus is waiting just ahead,

125
00:07:27,420 --> 00:07:31,280
so as to give you two,
who lack exercise daily, a little workout,

126
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:33,900
you'll be going by bicycle.

127
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:35,184
We, the entire staff,

128
00:07:35,234 --> 00:07:38,260
have considered your health, you see.

129
00:07:38,760 --> 00:07:40,520
Enough. Understood, understood.

130
00:07:40,740 --> 00:07:42,980
So Ryotsu is going to guide us?

131
00:07:43,280 --> 00:07:44,976
Yes. Your humble servant, Kankichi Ryotsu,

132
00:07:45,026 --> 00:07:48,520
will serve as tour conductor for this trip.

133
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:53,840
Ryotsu, is the bus still not here?

134
00:07:53,840 --> 00:07:56,220
It's just a little more,
only a little bit more.

135
00:07:57,600 --> 00:07:59,460
What do you mean "a little bit"?

136
00:07:59,460 --> 00:08:02,060
Haven't we been driving for
over 30 minutes now, Ohara?

137
00:08:02,060 --> 00:08:04,558
Well...

138
00:08:04,608 --> 00:08:10,980
That was close.

139
00:08:10,980 --> 00:08:13,660
We just barely made it in
time for the bus departure.

140
00:08:15,840 --> 00:08:17,160
Where are the seats?

141
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:20,840
That's odd. There's no seat H-9 or H-10.

142
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:24,880
Found it!
I see, it's a seat that fits the budget.

143
00:08:25,200 --> 00:08:27,740
Chief, Section Chief, this way please.

144
00:08:28,740 --> 00:08:29,820
Folding seats?

145
00:08:30,060 --> 00:08:33,240
Isn't it nostalgic? It's just like
an elementary school field trip.

146
00:08:47,160 --> 00:08:49,380
With the traffic lights and all,
I'm going to catch a cold...

147
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:51,340
Ryotsu, Ryotsu!

148
00:08:51,700 --> 00:08:52,700
Yes, what is it?

149
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:55,380
How long until we reach the destination?

150
00:08:55,760 --> 00:08:58,660
Well, it looks like we'll
arrive at 6 tomorrow morning.

151
00:08:59,120 --> 00:09:00,260
6 o'clock!?

152
00:09:00,260 --> 00:09:02,200
So we're going to sleep here, then.

153
00:09:02,220 --> 00:09:03,580
My back is going to hurt.

154
00:09:06,060 --> 00:09:07,660
Well, isn't that amazing? That.

155
00:09:15,740 --> 00:09:17,120
Midori, want some snacks?

156
00:09:17,580 --> 00:09:17,940
Thanks.

157
00:09:18,920 --> 00:09:20,060
There's beer, you know.

158
00:09:21,700 --> 00:09:23,280
Give me some Shi-kama too.

159
00:09:23,280 --> 00:09:23,840
Here you go.

160
00:09:25,240 --> 00:09:26,120
Here you go, senpai.

161
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:27,560
Put it on the seat over there.

162
00:09:27,560 --> 00:09:28,700
Got it, got it.

163
00:09:29,160 --> 00:09:31,960
I'd like to use the restroom.

164
00:09:33,040 --> 00:09:33,760
Yeah, yeah.

165
00:09:34,720 --> 00:09:35,440
Go ahead.

166
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:40,380
Can't settle down, can we, Chief?

167
00:09:42,340 --> 00:09:43,460
It's the invited trip today.

168
00:09:43,460 --> 00:09:45,020
Hey everybody

169
00:09:45,840 --> 00:09:47,700
Thanks for riding the ski bus.

170
00:09:48,360 --> 00:09:50,860
Please enjoy this trip to the fullest.

171
00:09:50,860 --> 00:09:51,540
Nice to meet you.

172
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:56,060
Mixed in with the young snowboarders,

173
00:09:56,060 --> 00:09:58,480
there are adult boarders here too,
aren't there?

174
00:09:59,240 --> 00:10:00,340
Since this is rare,

175
00:10:00,340 --> 00:10:02,580
maybe I'll ask you to introduce yourself,
if you don't mind.

176
00:10:02,580 --> 00:10:04,140
Could you pass the mic?

177
00:10:05,760 --> 00:10:08,380
This is sudden, and I'm a bit flustered.

178
00:10:08,960 --> 00:10:10,420
I'm Katsushika.

179
00:10:12,340 --> 00:10:18,020
Without some kind of introduction, it'd ruin the whole mood.
Right, so then, what should we call him?

180
00:10:18,500 --> 00:10:25,800
Eeh, this is the president of a near-bankrupt company, Mr. Tondayone.
If he issues another kite check, the company goes under instantly.

181
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:28,680
Everyone, please call him Mr. Sunawatari,
the Sand-Crossing President.

182
00:10:28,680 --> 00:10:37,780
Aaah, this is Daijiro Ohara, a freshly
laid-off, still-steaming Fresh Poo-Taro.

183
00:10:37,780 --> 00:10:40,860
Everyone,
please call him Mr. Future-Is-Pitch-Black.

184
00:10:41,320 --> 00:10:44,440
And this guy here got fired from
the company for embezzling money,

185
00:10:44,440 --> 00:10:48,040
and he's a good-for-nothing who runs from his creditors.
His name is Ryotsu Kankishi.

186
00:10:48,040 --> 00:10:50,840
Everyone,
please call him Mr. No Longer Human.

187
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:52,520
Mr. No Longer Human!

188
00:10:52,880 --> 00:10:54,540
Mr. Future-Is-Pitch-Black!

189
00:10:54,600 --> 00:10:55,100
Next topic!

190
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:00,720
Isn't this going well?

191
00:11:00,720 --> 00:11:03,120
Chief, now's your moment for a dad joke!

192
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:03,980
You're really going to do it?

193
00:11:03,980 --> 00:11:06,160
That'll send your popularity soaring again!

194
00:11:07,780 --> 00:11:09,700
Friday's side dish is... FRY-day!

195
00:11:15,280 --> 00:11:16,660
This is bad, Chief.

196
00:11:16,660 --> 00:11:17,840
Everyone's cringing.

197
00:11:17,840 --> 00:11:19,560
It's freezing in here.

198
00:11:19,560 --> 00:11:22,080
Let's bring out the chief, our headliner,

199
00:11:22,080 --> 00:11:23,660
for a comeback punchline.

200
00:11:23,660 --> 00:11:24,340
Is he really going to say it?

201
00:11:24,340 --> 00:11:26,500
Something that'll grab everyone's hearts,

202
00:11:26,500 --> 00:11:28,460
a powerful punchline, please.

203
00:11:30,220 --> 00:11:31,740
The futon blew away!

204
00:11:36,140 --> 00:11:37,240
The cat's sick in bed.

205
00:11:40,560 --> 00:11:42,560
I heard they built a
fence around the back base.

206
00:11:42,560 --> 00:11:45,180
A little joke from heaven.

207
00:11:45,180 --> 00:11:47,680
Escaping from the afterlife...

208
00:11:47,680 --> 00:11:48,780
Nobody called for you.

209
00:11:48,780 --> 00:11:50,800
My apologies.

210
00:12:11,640 --> 00:12:12,740
Excuse me.

211
00:12:12,740 --> 00:12:14,280
Please move.

212
00:12:14,280 --> 00:12:15,440
I need the restroom.

213
00:12:16,700 --> 00:12:17,780
Yeah, yeah.

214
00:12:20,940 --> 00:12:22,700
I can't sleep at all.

215
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:24,720
Where's Gyōtsu?

216
00:12:29,860 --> 00:12:31,320
Someplace like that.

217
00:12:31,320 --> 00:12:33,340
He can sleep anywhere.

218
00:12:35,140 --> 00:12:36,940
It's a silver-white world.

219
00:12:37,880 --> 00:12:41,340
What a refreshing morning
after a good long sleep.

220
00:12:41,340 --> 00:12:43,360
I'm sleepy and my head hurts.

221
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:45,760
We were woken up every ten minutes,
you know.

222
00:12:46,240 --> 00:12:50,000
Katsushika Police Box party,
we'll now show you to your lodgings.

223
00:12:50,700 --> 00:12:52,880
Your accommodations are this way.

224
00:12:54,180 --> 00:12:56,667
I heard it was a first-class
hot spring hotel, but...

225
00:12:56,717 --> 00:12:58,780
It's not bad, is it, Chief?

226
00:12:58,780 --> 00:13:02,440
Well, we can't be picky.
It's fine, it's fine.

227
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:04,300
Well, actually, there's one problem.

228
00:13:04,980 --> 00:13:07,880
You'll be sharing a room
with eight of those guys.

229
00:13:07,880 --> 00:13:08,260
What?

230
00:13:16,360 --> 00:13:19,280
Ryotsu, can't we get a room just for us?

231
00:13:19,460 --> 00:13:19,814
Well,

232
00:13:19,864 --> 00:13:23,500
this time of year is packed with skiers,
so it'll be tough.

233
00:13:23,500 --> 00:13:26,180
But with such troublesome people...

234
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:27,800
Right, Chief.

235
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:30,060
Understood, I'll go negotiate.

236
00:13:31,660 --> 00:13:33,840
No money, but you want us to let you stay?

237
00:13:34,300 --> 00:13:37,187
Yes, actually,
we lost our money on the way here,

238
00:13:37,237 --> 00:13:39,000
and we're in dire straits.

239
00:13:39,260 --> 00:13:42,860
As long as we're sheltered from the rain and wind,
we don't mind anywhere, even a horse stable.

240
00:13:43,100 --> 00:13:45,980
Please, have mercy.
Just one night's lodging, we beg you.

241
00:13:46,140 --> 00:13:48,480
Really, anywhere will do?

242
00:13:48,760 --> 00:13:50,940
Yes, if you'd be so kind as to grant it.

243
00:13:51,500 --> 00:13:54,320
Chief, Section Chief, it's OK.

244
00:13:55,040 --> 00:13:56,200
That's good news.

245
00:13:56,300 --> 00:13:57,440
Yes, really, really.

246
00:13:59,740 --> 00:14:02,180
They say we can use this storehouse.

247
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:09,280
You can say that about this idiot.

248
00:14:09,280 --> 00:14:11,640
But this is better, no need to hold back.

249
00:14:11,640 --> 00:14:13,460
Well, that's true, but...

250
00:14:13,460 --> 00:14:16,600
Ryotsu-kun, what's happening with our meals?

251
00:14:16,600 --> 00:14:18,960
Yes, yes, I'll go ask right now.

252
00:14:19,540 --> 00:14:19,940
What?

253
00:14:20,460 --> 00:14:21,760
Demanding they feed us too.

254
00:14:21,760 --> 00:14:25,480
Yes! We've had no food or drink for three days and three nights.
We're at our limit.

255
00:14:25,480 --> 00:14:27,900
We're about to die.
Please, we're begging you.

256
00:14:27,900 --> 00:14:31,680
We'll pay you back later,
or work it off, whatever it takes.

257
00:14:32,220 --> 00:14:33,220
Well then...

258
00:14:34,300 --> 00:14:35,200
And let us into the hot spring too.

259
00:14:40,740 --> 00:14:43,240
Ryo-san, what on earth is going on?

260
00:14:43,240 --> 00:14:45,180
Why are we having to do this?

261
00:14:45,180 --> 00:14:48,180
Well, it seems the rumor has spread
that we're people who got laid off.

262
00:14:48,180 --> 00:14:50,200
that we're people who got laid off.

263
00:14:50,200 --> 00:14:53,340
So the inn staff kindly said,
"You must be in trouble, aren't you?

264
00:14:53,340 --> 00:14:56,900
If you like, why don't you work here?"

265
00:14:56,900 --> 00:15:00,200
Can I really refuse when
they say that, Chief?

266
00:15:01,260 --> 00:15:02,620
Can you refuse, Chief?

267
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:08,060
Come on, stop wasting time
with idle talk and hurry up.

268
00:15:09,960 --> 00:15:11,180
Just tell me when you're listening.

269
00:15:13,440 --> 00:15:14,900
Next is the plum room.

270
00:15:23,280 --> 00:15:25,920
They say we can eat, too.

271
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:28,040
Thank you for the meal.

272
00:15:35,280 --> 00:15:39,100
Well, a meal after manual
labor really is delicious.

273
00:15:39,100 --> 00:15:40,500
Yes, really, really.

274
00:15:40,500 --> 00:15:41,932
Well, that's good.

275
00:15:41,982 --> 00:15:44,800
There's plenty more manual
labor coming after this.

276
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:06,380
Alright, alright, alright,
let's go to the bath.

277
00:16:06,380 --> 00:16:07,460
The bath.

278
00:16:09,760 --> 00:16:17,160
Well, they said once the cleaning's done we can use the bath too, so that's fine, right?
But this isn't much of a company retreat at all, is it?

279
00:16:17,160 --> 00:16:20,600
Anyway, let's get this over with quickly.

280
00:16:20,600 --> 00:16:21,000
That's right.

281
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:25,260
Ugh...

282
00:16:31,460 --> 00:16:34,460
You guys were on the bus,
and this old man...

283
00:16:34,460 --> 00:16:35,560
You nosy snoop.

284
00:16:35,560 --> 00:16:36,200
Pervert.

285
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:37,360
Sick.

286
00:16:37,360 --> 00:16:38,800
We're not that kind of people,

287
00:16:38,800 --> 00:16:39,800
cleaning

288
00:16:39,800 --> 00:16:40,500
we're doing.

289
00:16:47,520 --> 00:16:48,760
What a nuisance, isn't it.

290
00:16:48,760 --> 00:16:49,780
Honestly.

291
00:16:49,780 --> 00:16:51,720
I'm terribly sorry.

292
00:16:51,720 --> 00:16:54,260
We're banning you from our bath, you know.

293
00:16:54,260 --> 00:16:54,660
No way.

294
00:16:54,660 --> 00:16:57,440
To come all this way and not be
able to bathe in the hot spring!

295
00:16:57,440 --> 00:17:00,120
You brought it on yourselves,
so it can't be helped, yeah.

296
00:17:06,260 --> 00:17:08,920
This has turned into a miserable trip,
hasn't it.

297
00:17:08,920 --> 00:17:10,100
Honestly.

298
00:17:10,540 --> 00:17:11,700
Chief, Chief!

299
00:17:12,320 --> 00:17:14,840
Come on, let's go soak in the hot spring!

300
00:17:15,840 --> 00:17:18,700
But you're banned from the bath, remember?

301
00:17:18,700 --> 00:17:21,100
No, I got it out of a local, you see.

302
00:17:21,100 --> 00:17:25,580
Apparently there's a famous hot spring up this
back mountain where you can bathe for free.

303
00:17:25,580 --> 00:17:27,980
Come on, let's go right away, let's go!

304
00:17:34,640 --> 00:17:37,240
Is it really out here somewhere?

305
00:17:37,240 --> 00:17:40,400
The famous hot spring is quite a ways off,
you know.

306
00:17:40,400 --> 00:17:43,820
No wonder it's free to get in, really.

307
00:17:45,700 --> 00:17:47,780
There are avalanches around here, too.

308
00:17:49,060 --> 00:17:51,420
Move, move!

309
00:17:51,720 --> 00:17:53,160
Whoa! It's hot!

310
00:17:58,620 --> 00:17:59,700
Kakurabujaa!

311
00:18:00,860 --> 00:18:02,700
Hey! That's dangerous!

312
00:18:03,040 --> 00:18:04,740
The Pervert Uncle Squad!

313
00:18:04,900 --> 00:18:07,840
Ah, this is a no-snowboarding zone!

314
00:18:07,960 --> 00:18:09,860
Ski on the slopes, on the slopes!

315
00:18:10,300 --> 00:18:11,180
Let's go, let's go!

316
00:18:11,260 --> 00:18:11,760
What?!

317
00:18:11,860 --> 00:18:14,080
Nozokima, Distral, Erason...

318
00:18:14,080 --> 00:18:15,700
Ski on the slopes, you hear me!

319
00:18:15,700 --> 00:18:17,100
Yeah, yeah.

320
00:18:18,820 --> 00:18:21,280
Well, it's just a little further, let's go.

321
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:22,740
That's creepy.

322
00:18:27,300 --> 00:18:28,420
Is this it?

323
00:18:29,340 --> 00:18:30,960
Someone's already in there

324
00:18:32,940 --> 00:18:34,960
If it's girls, that'd be bad, right?

325
00:18:34,960 --> 00:18:36,560
This is the mixed-bathing spot.

326
00:18:40,680 --> 00:18:41,800
Whoa.

327
00:18:43,020 --> 00:18:44,920
Pardon us.

328
00:18:46,480 --> 00:18:51,080
Monkey and Mackie, tonight...

329
00:18:54,320 --> 00:18:56,920
Then, the other one...

330
00:18:56,920 --> 00:18:57,500
Mm.

331
00:19:01,740 --> 00:19:03,700
Hey, Chief, you go ahead too.

332
00:19:04,320 --> 00:19:04,860
Mm.

333
00:19:06,540 --> 00:19:08,140
Then pass it around.

334
00:19:39,300 --> 00:19:40,820
Where's Midori? Midori's not here.

335
00:19:41,220 --> 00:19:43,740
What? Did she get caught in it?

336
00:19:44,380 --> 00:19:46,640
Where was she when she got caught in it?

337
00:19:47,640 --> 00:19:49,320
Think back, quick!

338
00:19:49,320 --> 00:19:51,940
She was sliding right behind me.

339
00:19:51,940 --> 00:19:52,940
Roughly where?

340
00:19:53,060 --> 00:19:54,140
I think it was over around there.

341
00:19:54,560 --> 00:19:54,880
Okay.

342
00:19:56,900 --> 00:19:57,540
Are you all right?

343
00:19:58,680 --> 00:19:59,600
Answer me!

344
00:20:01,460 --> 00:20:02,940
Hey, can you hear me?

345
00:20:03,880 --> 00:20:05,920
We should contact the local police.

346
00:20:06,780 --> 00:20:09,640
If you're caught in an avalanche,
15 minutes is the most you've got.

347
00:20:10,140 --> 00:20:13,220
15 minutes?
If 15 minutes pass, will Midori die?

348
00:20:13,660 --> 00:20:13,980
No way.

349
00:20:14,780 --> 00:20:18,980
Don't panic! I'll find her, no matter what.
You two, believe in her and search too.

350
00:20:19,400 --> 00:20:19,720
Yes.

351
00:20:27,720 --> 00:20:32,160
She's not here. Maybe she was swept downhill,
or to the other side.

352
00:20:32,160 --> 00:20:33,720
Ten minutes have already passed.

353
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:38,320
Do you know her cell phone number?

354
00:20:50,280 --> 00:20:51,200
There she is!

355
00:20:53,900 --> 00:20:54,940
Midori!

356
00:20:59,540 --> 00:21:00,780
Is she okay? She's breathing.

357
00:21:01,420 --> 00:21:02,660
Hey, hang in there!

358
00:21:03,440 --> 00:21:06,499
Ah ah ah ah...

359
00:21:06,549 --> 00:21:09,898
Ah ah ah ah...

360
00:21:09,948 --> 00:21:13,273
Ah ah ah ah...

361
00:21:13,323 --> 00:21:16,698
Ah ah ah ah...

362
00:21:16,748 --> 00:21:20,061
Ah ah ah ah...

363
00:21:20,111 --> 00:21:23,473
Ah ah ah ah...

364
00:21:23,523 --> 00:21:26,861
Ah ah ah ah...

365
00:21:26,911 --> 00:21:30,420
Ah ah ah ah...

366
00:21:34,860 --> 00:21:36,760
It's been a long day, hasn't it.

367
00:21:37,200 --> 00:21:41,260
Doesn't a snowy day like this
bring back memories, Chief?

368
00:21:41,260 --> 00:21:44,480
Yes, I was just thinking the same thing.

369
00:21:44,480 --> 00:21:48,880
We couldn't give up on that unsolved case,
so the two of us investigated it together.

370
00:21:48,880 --> 00:21:52,020
We both had a strong
sense of justice back then.

371
00:21:54,120 --> 00:21:55,100
We were the police.

372
00:21:57,760 --> 00:22:00,500
Looking back, we were pretty reckless.

373
00:22:01,080 --> 00:22:03,820
The case was reinvestigated and
the suspect was convicted, but...

374
00:22:03,820 --> 00:22:07,320
If we'd been wrong,
we'd both have been fired.

375
00:22:08,220 --> 00:22:10,520
We were young, weren't we.

376
00:22:11,600 --> 00:22:13,580
Youth was our only weapon.

377
00:22:14,900 --> 00:22:15,380
Yes.

378
00:22:16,660 --> 00:22:17,640
Good evening.

379
00:22:21,640 --> 00:22:24,560
Thank you for helping me earlier.

380
00:22:25,520 --> 00:22:27,780
And I said a lot of rude things.

381
00:22:27,780 --> 00:22:29,400
I'm really sorry.

382
00:22:29,400 --> 00:22:32,500
It's fine, Ohara-kun.

383
00:22:32,500 --> 00:22:34,800
I'm not upset about it anymore.

384
00:22:39,520 --> 00:22:42,020
They're such reliable people, aren't they?

385
00:22:42,020 --> 00:22:46,840
Yes, being able to act so calmly in
that situation is truly admirable.

386
00:22:47,440 --> 00:22:50,480
Could you possibly be
police officers in reality?

387
00:22:51,580 --> 00:22:52,020
No,

388
00:22:52,020 --> 00:22:52,340
No-

389
00:22:53,020 --> 00:22:54,200
I'm sure you are.

390
00:22:54,200 --> 00:22:55,960
You were keeping it a secret because of your duties,
weren't you?

391
00:22:55,960 --> 00:22:58,060
No, let's broadcast that instead.

392
00:22:58,060 --> 00:22:59,300
What should we do, I wonder?

393
00:23:02,680 --> 00:23:05,980
Lately, we...

394
00:23:07,300 --> 00:23:08,460
Nice.

395
00:23:09,400 --> 00:23:10,640
Sorry about that.

396
00:23:11,400 --> 00:23:12,540
Thank you so much.

397
00:23:12,540 --> 00:23:16,160
Please keep looking after us from now on.

398
00:23:17,300 --> 00:23:20,440
Here, take some of the fruit.

399
00:23:25,280 --> 00:23:26,720
Welcome back.

400
00:23:27,260 --> 00:23:28,500
I'm back.

401
00:23:28,500 --> 00:23:30,260
This is a souvenir, you know.

402
00:23:32,060 --> 00:23:34,540
So, how was the trip?

403
00:23:34,540 --> 00:23:37,460
We did karaoke with some college girls.

404
00:23:37,460 --> 00:23:40,040
It was a fun ski bus tour, wasn't it?

405
00:23:40,660 --> 00:23:42,080
"Ski bus"?

406
00:23:42,880 --> 00:23:45,580
Well, it was a fun trip, wasn't it?

407
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:47,420
By the way, where's Ryo-san?

408
00:23:57,680 --> 00:23:59,980
Ugh, on the way, ueeeee...

409
00:24:00,980 --> 00:24:05,500
Kicking the alarm clock away,
my little toe goes ouch, ouch, ouch.

410
00:24:05,500 --> 00:24:13,900
Just draw on my eyebrows,
then dash, dash, dash to the station.

411
00:24:13,900 --> 00:24:19,400
Packed train, yeah,
a quick nap on the way home.

412
00:24:20,520 --> 00:24:25,700
Another tough week,
overwork is only natural.

413
00:24:27,000 --> 00:24:30,540
Bucket in hand, playing it cool.

414
00:24:30,540 --> 00:24:33,360
Beef bowl, extra sauce, extra soupy.

415
00:24:33,880 --> 00:24:36,620
Even the irritation from endless overtime.

416
00:24:36,620 --> 00:24:40,220
Irritation blown away, feeling refreshed.

417
00:24:43,600 --> 00:24:46,040
Every day's no-problem-

418
00:24:46,040 --> 00:24:50,040
After passing through the hot shower,

419
00:24:50,040 --> 00:24:53,180
every day's no-problem-brain.

420
00:24:53,180 --> 00:24:56,600
Energy restored with a sound-sleep pillow.

421
00:24:59,660 --> 00:25:02,720
Every day's no-problem-brain.

422
00:25:02,720 --> 00:25:06,200
I love a girl like me.

423
00:25:06,200 --> 00:25:09,400
Every day's no-problem-brain.

424
00:25:09,400 --> 00:25:13,020
Monday, with hearts flying everywhere.

425
00:25:13,020 --> 00:25:16,520
Andeck, Andeck, no-problem-

426
00:25:19,820 --> 00:25:21,820
You mean Shinobazu Pond in Ueno?

427
00:25:21,820 --> 00:25:24,360
It was my playground since I was a kid.

428
00:25:24,360 --> 00:25:26,020
Let's go take a boat out or something.

429
00:25:26,500 --> 00:25:30,040
A toy submarine from the bottom of the pond?

430
00:25:30,620 --> 00:25:33,600
Could this be from when I was a kid?

431
00:25:33,600 --> 00:25:37,360
Next time, tell me more about
your Shinobazu Pond memories, okay?

